\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Signed effects, raw and standardized (\,$\beta /\mathrm  {SD}(Y)$, which makes the panels comparable\,). On the common scale the \textbf  {complete detector's} elicitation response is both large and tightly consistent ($+1.27$ to $+1.56$\,SD) while its content response changes sign; the single feature's elicitation response is smaller and itself sign-unstable. Both panels are OLS; claim-pair clustered CIs, $B\!=\!2000$.}}{5}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
